<body>
    <h1>AIP-159: Implement versioning system for AI+ Utilities</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>It=E2=80=99s high-time we implement a versioning system to keep =
ourselves straight.</p>
<p>To implement a versioning system for Python projects on GitHub with auto=
-incremented versioning, TeamCity builds, and AWS ECR deployment, here=E2=
=80=99s a detailed step-by-step guide:</p>
<h1 id=3D"AIP-159:ImplementversioningsystemforAI+Utilities-VersioningStrate=
gy">Versioning Strategy</h1>
<p>For AI+ projects, we will use the basic semantic versioning practices <s=
trong>(MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)</strong> with an additional <strong>build number<=
/strong>. We will track :</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>MAJOR</strong> for new releases a scoped release</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>MINOR</strong> for new features within</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>PATCH</strong> for bug fixes within a release.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>BUILD</strong> for each TeamCity build</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p>MAJOR, MINOR, and PATCH releases will be manually committed with a PR. I=
t will be the job of the committer and pull request viewer to ensure the ve=
rsioning info is updated as part of the review process. BUILD numbers will =
be managed by the TeamCity CI/CD pipeline.</p>
<h1 id=3D"AIP-159:ImplementversioningsystemforAI+Utilities-AI+Utilities">AI=
+ Utilities</h1>
<p>Each project will have a setup.py: We will include a __version__ variabl=
e that reads from a version file.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">from setu=
ptools import setup

# Read version from a version file
with open("VERSION") as version_file:
    version =3D version_file.read().strip()

setup(
    name=3D"your_project",
    version=3Dversion,
    # other parameters
)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<p>The version file itself is very basic.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: plain; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Vers=
ioning follows the format: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-BUILD
# Only one line should be present in this file, e.g., 1.0.0-0
1.0.0-0</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"AIP-159:ImplementversioningsystemforAI+Utilities-TeamCity">TeamCi=
ty</h1>
<p>As part of the build process, we will use a Python script to update the =
version and build number in a <code>VERSION</code> file. Here=E2=80=99s an =
example script:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import re

# File name where the current version is stored
VERSION_FILE =3D "VERSION"

def increment_version(version_file=3DVERSION_FILE):
    """
    Reads the current version from the VERSION file, increments the build n=
umber,
    and writes the new version back to the VERSION file.

    Version format: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-BUILD
    - MAJOR, MINOR, and PATCH should be updated manually for significant re=
leases.
    - BUILD is auto-incremented on every build.
    """
    # Open and read the current version
    with open(version_file, "r") as file:
        version =3D file.read().strip()
   =20
    # Use regular expressions to parse version components
    # Assumes format: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-BUILD
    major, minor, patch, build =3D map(int, re.match(r"(\d+)\.(\d+)\.(\d+)-=
(\d+)", version).groups())
   =20
    # Increment the build number for the next version
    build +=3D 1
    new_version =3D f"{major}.{minor}.{patch}-{build}"

    # Write the new version back to the VERSION file
    with open(version_file, "w") as file:
        file.write(new_version)
   =20
    # Display the updated version
    print(f"Updated version to {new_version}")

# Entry point for the script, which increments the version
if __name__ =3D=3D "__main__":
    increment_version()</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>We will run this script in TeamCity=E2=80=99s build steps to update the =
version before every build.</p>
<p>In the TeamCity build configuration:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Run the version update script as a step.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Commit and tag the updated version.</p></li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"AIP-159:ImplementversioningsystemforAI+Utilities-TeamCityBuildSte=
ps:">TeamCity Build Steps:</h4>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Increment Version Step</strong>: Run the versioning script above=
.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Git Commit Step</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">git con=
fig user.email "teamcity@datacore.com"
git config user.name "TeamCity"
git commit -am "Auto-incremented version to $(cat VERSION)"</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Git Tag Step</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">VERSION=
=3D$(cat VERSION)
git tag -a "v$VERSION" -m "Build $VERSION"
git push origin --tags</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"AIP-159:ImplementversioningsystemforAI+Utilities-IntegrateDockerB=
uildandPushtoAWSECR">Integrate Docker Build and Push to AWS ECR</h3>
<p>In TeamCity, add steps to:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Build Docker Image</strong>: Use the version as a tag.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">VERSION=
=3D$(cat VERSION)
docker build -t aiplus/notification-api:$VERSION .</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Push to ECR</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Log i=
n to ECR
aws ecr get-login-password --region us-east-1 | docker login --username AWS=
 --password-stdin &lt;accountId&gt;.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
docker tag aiplus/notification-api:$VERSION &lt;accountId&gt;.dkr.ecr.your-=
region.amazonaws.com/aiplus/notification-api:$VERSION
docker push &lt;accountId&gt;.dkr.ecr.your-region.amazonaws.com/aiplus/noti=
fication-api:$VERSION</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"AIP-159:ImplementversioningsystemforAI+Utilities-AWSECR">AWS ECR<=
/h3>
<p>To keep storage manageable, we should implement a lifecycle policy in AW=
S ECR to delete old images.</p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
